From c1e61fcc4ace18bd5073c63deb37d4a192ddc9b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alemar <6304136+darkguy2008@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:54:13 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] backend/drm: ignore empty legacy CRTC mode

nouveau reads a CRTC the firmware left lit back as enabled with no mode:
its nv50_display_read_hw_or_state() sets the head state's enable and
active but never the mode. Through the legacy API, drmModeGetCrtc then
reports mode_valid with an all-zero mode, and connect_drm_connector()
passes it to calculate_refresh_rate(), which divides by htotal and
kills the compositor with SIGFPE on every start.

Treat a mode whose totals are zero as no current mode, as the kernel's
drm_mode_vrefresh() does.
---
 backend/drm/drm.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/backend/drm/drm.c b/backend/drm/drm.c
index 054c24a..11961fa 100644
--- a/backend/drm/drm.c
+++ b/backend/drm/drm.c
@@ -1572,7 +1572,10 @@ static drmModeModeInfo *connector_get_current_mode(struct wlr_drm_connector *wlr
 			wlr_log_errno(WLR_ERROR, "drmModeGetCrtc failed");
 			return NULL;
 		}
-		if (!drm_crtc->mode_valid) {
+		// nouveau reads back a firmware-lit CRTC as enabled with an empty
+		// mode, and the refresh rate of a mode divides by its totals
+		if (!drm_crtc->mode_valid || drm_crtc->mode.htotal == 0 ||
+				drm_crtc->mode.vtotal == 0) {
 			drmModeFreeCrtc(drm_crtc);
 			return NULL;
 		}
